<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The one capability the app claims. Screen 1's "Continue with Apple" is the only route in
	  that does not depend on mail being delivered, and without this key the sheet never opens:
	  ASAuthorizationController answers .unknown before it draws anything.

	  "Default" means this app's own App ID is the audience — a native iOS client, so no Services
	  ID and no client secret. `com.cjgimena.app` goes in the Supabase dashboard as the Apple
	  provider's Client ID and that is the whole server side of it.

	  It was `org.sycamore.app` up to 2026-08-06, from the original scaffold. That identifier was
	  never registered with Apple — the scaffold set no DEVELOPMENT_TEAM, so it only ever built
	  for the simulator, which signs ad-hoc and registers nothing. Nothing was claimed and
	  nothing had to be released.

	  This file lives in `Config/` rather than beside the app's other resources, and that is
	  deliberate. `Sycamore/` is a synchronised root group, which takes everything under it into
	  the target by default — so here it would ship inside the .app as a plain-text claim, and
	  the only thing preventing that was one `membershipExceptions` line that Xcode deleted on
	  four separate occasions without a word. Out here there is nothing to except. It is read by
	  path, through CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS, which never wanted target membership in the first
	  place.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
